To the Public Records Officers of the State of Oregon:

On March 3, 2026, I wrote 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01KJT9T6V8Q8PATA3JMZ8DD1ZW/> 
Deputy Director J.R. Collier of Oregon Parks and Recreation Department. 
I told him I was working two jobs and volunteering for the US Forest 
Service. I told him I intended to secure the funds to sue his agency for 
barring me from participating in civic government. And I told him there 
was still time to prevent it. It was the last door I was holding open 
for the man and I told him as much. I ended with refusal: "You will not 
bury this."

He reached for borrowed power.

Within hours, a man I have never met or corresponded with, using a title 
meant to carry the entire act, Oregon State Parks' Emergency Manager 
Jamen Lee, copying Deputy Director J.R. Collier, wrote 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/records/osp/attachments/01m1m4wf78xjpejj48d1jz4sj8-Electronic-Communications-Electronic-Communications.pdf#page=2> 
to the press captain at Oregon State Police. He did not allege a crime 
or a threat. He sent the other man a link to my archive and invoked his 
Director and our Governor as justification.

>From that moment forward, I became a target of your state government's 
police power.

I was targeted and documented by the people you work for. My name was 
placed in state and federal criminal databases. My supervisor was told 
not to inform me law enforcement was looking for me. And three men with 
guns showed up at my door to tell me I was "not in trouble." Behind a 
locked gate, at a secured federal facility, in a forest, on the 
anniversary the Deputy's agency displaced me from the life I built from 
scratch. Days after they left, someone left a box of spent shotgun 
shells at my gate, covered in urine.

I responded to this very serious abuse of power by asking for the public 
records of these events. I have followed every channel the government 
created to repair an act like this one, and discovered every channel 
pointed at containment and away from public disclosure or accountability.

This includes you. If you disagree, say so now.

I am a United States citizen. That alone afforded me the right not to be 
intimidated at my home and workplace over my public speech. And it 
affords me the right to see who did it and why. This matter now sits 
before your Public Records Advocate as the final test of what this state 
government does when it harms someone.

This weekend, I finished a feature called Key Individuals 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/key-individuals/> to the archive. It 
lists three categories of dozens of individuals and offices, including 
yours. It is my considered point of view that no one who exercises force 
or holds responsibility for that use of force should ever be concealed 
from public examination. It is my further opinion that public records 
officers should be held to the highest possible standard and that by 
default everything they do should be on the record.

Despite the fact every one of you has failed to meet this standard, I 
have made the decision to focus this record on the ones I consider most 
dangerous, and that is anyone who wields power unethically and 
unaccountably, and that is not you, so your names are redacted.

*Robert Samuel White*
